hi there  steve kaufman here again today i want to  talk about  what i call a language learning toolbox  i had a comment on one of my um  youtube videos where i said that i  tried shadowing  which is a  method of language learning or an  activity whereby  you listen and speak out loud i don't i  don't want to go in detail on it because  i don't  i tried a little bit of sort of reading  and speaking out loud or whatever i  don't like i don't enjoy doing it you  can look it up shadowing language  learning you'll find it a lot of people  swear by fine i said i tried it i didn't  enjoy doing it and then people  criticized me and one person said you  know why are you so reluctant to add  this to your toolbox or something so  toolbox  if you are  a woodworker  then you have or in whatever you're a  stamp collector in any hobby  your tools are there in order to make  the main activity that enjoyable hobby  activity more efficient more enjoyable  but the  use of that tool the tool itself is not  the goal the tool is there to help you  do what you like to do  so  to me  an activity which is a tool like  shadowing  um doesn't appeal to me to me the  activity which appeals is using the  language so  listening reading speaking writing using  the language  is the activity that gives me enjoyment  the tools  um  i could say the resources i find on the  internet the  podcast that i find  my um  mp3 player my iphone my ipad link  dictionaries these are the tools  that help me  do the task which i enjoy doing which is  engaging with the language  so  uh  those sort of almost you know deliberate  learning strategy type tools  to me are not tools they're another  activity and for those people who enjoy  those activities then that's a great  thing to do because that's what they  enjoy doing  but the tool  is not the activity the activity to me  is is what engages me and  so i do those things which which i find  uh you know engage me have high  resonance and so forth  um  so that's  by 